{"id": "EUVD-2026-55272", "enisaUuid": "92d3d5d8-6703-396c-a701-e28e39f43bc2", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nHID: wacom: stop hardware after post-start probe failures\n\nwacom_parse_and_register() starts HID hardware before registering inputs\nand initializing pad LEDs/remotes. Those later steps can fail, but their\nerror paths currently release Wacom resources without stopping the HID\nhardware.\n\nRoute post-hid_hw_start() failures through hid_hw_stop() before\nreleasing driver resources.\n\nThis issue was identified during our ongoing static-analysis research while\nreviewing kernel code.", "datePublished": "2026-08-10T11:51:46", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T20:48:44", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5a7ca028facf04921b2c1c2e4d1ee7f282510555", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3e6473a4f0596182acdda5219b4bebfbee76514f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/46d8b8c85ae0589fb85746a64e8908160e52aac3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1a1ebdcb56ae58a0ee2c54dd15d75121e30424e3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/75eb2173b63ab41c24d80cd641af18f3c117a267", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/416095e9a6037b4b39fcadd0d2bd77a8852211ec", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e2cc711a9df37f359159b21db56cea9c21f58a9c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ec2612b8ad9e642596db011dd8b6568ef1edeaa1"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-68091", "GHSA-jmfj-p2w9-43g4"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.26, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0b4aeafa-e4d3-387d-a609-cdc390deba3f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.15.149 <5.15.212"}, {"id": "0c426d3e-1cb9-3809-bd11-a174cec71255", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "dbaca8fa9ec2c5aa55ec515686ce3b9007554eab"}, {"id": "0e485e30-00f9-3350-961c-43cf46e1c0d5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"